    "statementMarkdown": "The numbers from 1 to 360 are partitioned into 9 subsets of consecutive integers and the sums of the numbers in each subset are arranged in the cells of a $3 \\times 3$ square. Is it possible that the square turns out to be a magic square?\n\nRemark: A magic square is a square in which the sums of the numbers in each row, in each column and in both diagonals are all equal.\n",
